repository-code: "https://github.com/xiacy111111/abi-snp-analyzer"
abstract: >-
  ABI-SNP Analyzer is a free, open-source desktop application for automated
  SNP genotyping and population genetic analysis from Sanger sequencing
  chromatograms. It provides an end-to-end graphical workflow from raw Applied
  Biosystems .ab1 files to quality-control plots, IUPAC-coded sequences,
  multiple-sequence alignments, diploid genotype matrices, reference-genome
  coordinates, population genetic statistics, and data files for commonly used
  downstream software.
keywords:
  - SNP genotyping
  - population genetics
  - Sanger sequencing
  - chromatogram analysis
  - ABIF
  - IUPAC
  - F-statistics
  - AMOVA
  - Hardy-Weinberg equilibrium
type: software
